MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The router and Alexa-compatible cameras feel like useful additions to my connected home: better connectivity could support my devices, and the cameras connect with my earlier interest in home security.",
    "The portable WD drive complements my older desktop drive with storage I can move around. The docking station also interests me because I use many peripherals, provided it works with my computer and displays."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Another Echo display and a compact keyboard feel unnecessary after my recent Echo Show 5, stand, and full-size keyboard purchases. The compact keyboard also lacks the numeric keypad I recently chose.",
    "The SSD enclosure and Mini USB cable require specific equipment or connection needs I have not shown. Headphones and garage storage straps do not address a current need suggested by my purchases."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning Alexa devices seems to be treated as a reason to want any Alexa-related product, even when it duplicates something I just bought or serves a different purpose.",
    "My accessory purchases seem to imply interest in almost any cable, storage accessory, or organizer, although I usually buy these to solve a particular practical problem."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases matter: buying a display stand suggests I am setting up the display I already have, while choosing a full-size keyboard with a numeric keypad makes a compact replacement less appealing.",
    "Useful additions need to fit my existing equipment. A ready-to-use external drive has a clearer purpose for me than an enclosure needing a separate SSD, and a dock is only useful if its connections match my computer."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my connected-home and computer-accessory interests, but sometimes confuse useful additions with redundant replacements or accessories without an established need."
}
